From 33ce2ccf8dceacfe1d70aa50c6d591064c59fc88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grzegorz <grzegorz2047@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 03:24:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] D3D12.X: a GPU without feature level 12_0 is used at 11_0
 before WARP

The title's device (hle::d3d12x::real) and the launcher's GPU check
(preflight) asked each hardware adapter for feature level 12_0 only,
then took WARP at 11_0. vkd3d-proton on the PS5's RADV (under
prospero-win) refuses 12_0: the GPU has tiled resources tier 1 only
("Feature level 0xc000 is not supported"). XCL then ran on "WARP
(software renderer)", which DXVK's dxgi answered with the same GPU, so
it worked by accident and was reported as WARP; on Windows the same
fallback would have been the software renderer.

gpu::adapter::create_device() now asks every adapter for 12_0, then
every adapter for 11_0, then WARP, and both callers use it (they had
the same loop copied). A device below 12_0 says so in its name and in
the log. On a GPU that gives 12_0 nothing changes.

Test: first_device() picks an adapter that gives only 11_0 (asked at
12_0 first), and prefers a later adapter with 12_0 to an earlier one
with 11_0.

Measured on an RTX 3060 Laptop GPU, Windows 11, Rust 1.100 debug:
cargo test --workspace --no-fail-fast -- --test-threads=4: 976 passed,
1 failed, 45 ignored, 23 SKIPPED; the failure is
execute_indirect_reads_the_arguments_written_before_it, as on main on
this GPU. Not yet run on the PS5.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
